  "holistic_F_N": 1,
  "holistic_F_H": -1,
  "section_notes": "S1 requires reporting all thermal incidents to regulators within 24 hours, customer notice within 72 hours, and no delay during investigation. S2 mandates 55°C testing with a 5% failure limit, per-model results to regulators and customers but not public, and corrective action for exceedances. S3 requires remote shut-off on new units and retrofit within 6 years; S4 requires built-in fire suppression within 36 months. S5 mandates recall at 8 incidents per 100k with prompt customer notice and no phase-in."
